    <item>
      <title>Questions and Answers</title>
      <link>https://benfernandezmedia.github.io/help/qna/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://benfernandezmedia.github.io/help/qna/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;&lt;h2
  class=&#34;not-prose hx:text-4xl hx:font-bold hx:leading-none hx:tracking-tighter hx:md:text-3xl hx:py-2 hx:bg-clip-text hx:text-transparent hx:bg-gradient-to-r hx:from-gray-900 hx:to-gray-600 hx:dark:from-gray-100 hx:dark:to-gray-400&#34;
  
&gt;
  Regarding The Website
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;details class=&#34;hx:last-of-type:mb-0 hx:rounded-lg hx:bg-neutral-50 hx:dark:bg-neutral-800 hx:p-2 hx:mt-4 hx:group&#34; &gt;
  &lt;summary class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:cursor-pointer hx:select-none hx:list-none hx:p-1 hx:rounded-sm hx:transition-colors hx:hover:bg-gray-100 hx:dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 hx:before:mr-1 hx:before:inline-block hx:before:transition-transform hx:before:content-[&#39;&#39;] hx:dark:before:invert hx:rtl:before:rotate-180 hx:group-open:before:rotate-90&#34;&gt;
    &lt;strong class=&#34;hx:text-lg&#34;&gt;Q. You used to have a website powered by MkDocs Material, why replace it with Hugo and Hextra?&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:p-2 hx:overflow-hidden&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A:&lt;/strong&gt; Originally, I was considering re-opening the site with that engine but as MkDocs Material is being passed on to a new SSG called Zensical, it will take too long to setup the website.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hugo and Hextra was chosen as a alternative because I think Hugo is mostly faster to setup and Hextra was the theme that somehow matches some of my branding aesthetics in a way, if assumed. The purpose was creating the website that is basically simple, clean, easy to navigate, and of course…fast!&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;

&lt;details class=&#34;hx:last-of-type:mb-0 hx:rounded-lg hx:bg-neutral-50 hx:dark:bg-neutral-800 hx:p-2 hx:mt-4 hx:group&#34; &gt;
  &lt;summary class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:cursor-pointer hx:select-none hx:list-none hx:p-1 hx:rounded-sm hx:transition-colors hx:hover:bg-gray-100 hx:dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 hx:before:mr-1 hx:before:inline-block hx:before:transition-transform hx:before:content-[&#39;&#39;] hx:dark:before:invert hx:rtl:before:rotate-180 hx:group-open:before:rotate-90&#34;&gt;
    &lt;strong class=&#34;hx:text-lg&#34;&gt;Q. Will this site be mostly focused on the blog in the future?&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:p-2 hx:overflow-hidden&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A:&lt;/strong&gt; No, the website will have more pages aside from the blog page. But since its launch, it will be stuck with only the blog page until I think of what to add on the website.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To add more pages, I need to carefully learn more documentation of both Hugo and Hextra, with some additional documentation from W3Schools in regards to HTML and CSS if needed.&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;

&lt;details class=&#34;hx:last-of-type:mb-0 hx:rounded-lg hx:bg-neutral-50 hx:dark:bg-neutral-800 hx:p-2 hx:mt-4 hx:group&#34; &gt;
  &lt;summary class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:cursor-pointer hx:select-none hx:list-none hx:p-1 hx:rounded-sm hx:transition-colors hx:hover:bg-gray-100 hx:dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 hx:before:mr-1 hx:before:inline-block hx:before:transition-transform hx:before:content-[&#39;&#39;] hx:dark:before:invert hx:rtl:before:rotate-180 hx:group-open:before:rotate-90&#34;&gt;
    &lt;strong class=&#34;hx:text-lg&#34;&gt;Q. How often is the site updated?&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:p-2 hx:overflow-hidden&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A:&lt;/strong&gt; It&amp;rsquo;s depending on the pushes I commit on GitHub since the site is hosted on there. The site gets updated to commit fixes, improvements or updating the site configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If working on a major update, it can take like at least two or three weeks to work on and push it to GitHub.&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;h2
  class=&#34;not-prose hx:text-4xl hx:font-bold hx:leading-none hx:tracking-tighter hx:md:text-3xl hx:py-2 hx:bg-clip-text hx:text-transparent hx:bg-gradient-to-r hx:from-gray-900 hx:to-gray-600 hx:dark:from-gray-100 hx:dark:to-gray-400&#34;
  
&gt;
  Regarding Our Content
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;details class=&#34;hx:last-of-type:mb-0 hx:rounded-lg hx:bg-neutral-50 hx:dark:bg-neutral-800 hx:p-2 hx:mt-4 hx:group&#34; &gt;
  &lt;summary class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:cursor-pointer hx:select-none hx:list-none hx:p-1 hx:rounded-sm hx:transition-colors hx:hover:bg-gray-100 hx:dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 hx:before:mr-1 hx:before:inline-block hx:before:transition-transform hx:before:content-[&#39;&#39;] hx:dark:before:invert hx:rtl:before:rotate-180 hx:group-open:before:rotate-90&#34;&gt;
    &lt;strong class=&#34;hx:text-lg&#34;&gt;Q. What&amp;rsquo;s your stance on AI content?&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:p-2 hx:overflow-hidden&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://benfernandezmedia.github.io/images/aistance.webp&#34; alt=&#34;LessAIMoreHuman-NotByAI&#34;  loading=&#34;lazy&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A:&lt;/strong&gt; With all the respect, I am not anti-AI or such but I do know that most artists don’t tolerate AI-generated art that has been everywhere online. But to me, in order to ensure that all of my content is genuine, I always implement the badges from Not By AI and also follow the Less AI, More Human Creativity stance that I’ve designed. It’s a principle that to ensure that AI is respectfully used, I mainly use AI only for research, feedback, suggestions, and of course verification based on my behalf as a creator but I don’t use it to generate visuals and post them online as it can harm future artists for inspiration.&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;

&lt;details class=&#34;hx:last-of-type:mb-0 hx:rounded-lg hx:bg-neutral-50 hx:dark:bg-neutral-800 hx:p-2 hx:mt-4 hx:group&#34; &gt;
  &lt;summary class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:cursor-pointer hx:select-none hx:list-none hx:p-1 hx:rounded-sm hx:transition-colors hx:hover:bg-gray-100 hx:dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 hx:before:mr-1 hx:before:inline-block hx:before:transition-transform hx:before:content-[&#39;&#39;] hx:dark:before:invert hx:rtl:before:rotate-180 hx:group-open:before:rotate-90&#34;&gt;
    &lt;strong class=&#34;hx:text-lg&#34;&gt;Q. Are you open for paid art commissions or such?&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:p-2 hx:overflow-hidden&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A:&lt;/strong&gt; With all the respect, under some internal debate I faced, I made a decision to not do paid commissions. As an artist, commissions can take a lot of responsibility and time to reach a deadline. In the distant future, if even I did do paid commissions, it could have some advantages to earn some royalties of how much I charge for my art.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since I don’t do paid commission, as an artist, I continue to have full creative control based on my belief.&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;h2
  class=&#34;not-prose hx:text-4xl hx:font-bold hx:leading-none hx:tracking-tighter hx:md:text-3xl hx:py-2 hx:bg-clip-text hx:text-transparent hx:bg-gradient-to-r hx:from-gray-900 hx:to-gray-600 hx:dark:from-gray-100 hx:dark:to-gray-400&#34;
  
&gt;
  Regarding MediaPlay
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;details class=&#34;hx:last-of-type:mb-0 hx:rounded-lg hx:bg-neutral-50 hx:dark:bg-neutral-800 hx:p-2 hx:mt-4 hx:group&#34; &gt;
  &lt;summary class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:cursor-pointer hx:select-none hx:list-none hx:p-1 hx:rounded-sm hx:transition-colors hx:hover:bg-gray-100 hx:dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 hx:before:mr-1 hx:before:inline-block hx:before:transition-transform hx:before:content-[&#39;&#39;] hx:dark:before:invert hx:rtl:before:rotate-180 hx:group-open:before:rotate-90&#34;&gt;
    &lt;strong class=&#34;hx:text-lg&#34;&gt;Q. What is MediaPlay?&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:p-2 hx:overflow-hidden&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://benfernandezmedia.github.io/images/mediaplay/logo_banner.webp&#34; alt=&#34;MediaPlay Logo&#34;  loading=&#34;lazy&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A:&lt;/strong&gt; MediaPlay is a newsletter where one of our characters hosts and report on the news of what&amp;rsquo;s happening in the center of the digital entertainment world! Each issue will also cover news in the gaming, digital media, and also in the entertainment industry!&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;

&lt;details class=&#34;hx:last-of-type:mb-0 hx:rounded-lg hx:bg-neutral-50 hx:dark:bg-neutral-800 hx:p-2 hx:mt-4 hx:group&#34; &gt;
  &lt;summary class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:cursor-pointer hx:select-none hx:list-none hx:p-1 hx:rounded-sm hx:transition-colors hx:hover:bg-gray-100 hx:dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 hx:before:mr-1 hx:before:inline-block hx:before:transition-transform hx:before:content-[&#39;&#39;] hx:dark:before:invert hx:rtl:before:rotate-180 hx:group-open:before:rotate-90&#34;&gt;
    &lt;strong class=&#34;hx:text-lg&#34;&gt;Q. Where can I find new issues of the newsletter?&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:p-2 hx:overflow-hidden&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A:&lt;/strong&gt; To find new issues of MediaPlay, choose &lt;strong&gt;MediaPlay&lt;/strong&gt; on the navigation bar or look at the ticker on the homepage to see new issues!&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

